<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 3 November, from 361 to 1957.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">361 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,665 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantius II dies, leaving Julian sole emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> while marching against his cousin Julian, who became sole Roman emperor. Julian, the last pagan emperor, tried to revive traditional cults but was killed fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 363.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1090 CE <span class="tih-ago">936 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Rufus fails to seize Rouen from his brother Robert</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces loyal to the English king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england">William Rufus</a> tried and failed to take control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>, capital of his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a>, Duke of Normandy. In 1096 William took Normandy in pledge from Robert, who was leaving on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england">William II of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VII and Charles VIII make peace at Étaples</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Peace of Étaples ended Henry VII's brief invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>: Charles VIII paid him a large sum and agreed to stop supporting Yorkist pretenders. The treaty helped secure the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-tudor">Tudor dynasty</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1493">1493 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">533 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Columbus passes the island of Dominica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> is said to have passed Dominica, in the Lesser Antilles, an island then inhabited by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a>, who had displaced the earlier Arawak settlers. Europeans, mainly the French from 1690, later colonised it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Olympe de Gouges is guillotined</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The playwright Olympe de Gouges, author of the Declaration of the Rights of Woman and of the Female Citizen, was executed during the Terror for writings attacking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobin-club">Jacobins</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1839">1839 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">187 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British and Chinese warships clash at Chuenpi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> frigates fought Chinese war junks off Chuenpi near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Canton</a>, the first major clash of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a>. The dispute followed Lin Zexu's destruction of British merchants' opium; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> in 1842.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1867">1867 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French and papal troops defeat Garibaldi at Mentana</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Mentana, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, papal troops supported by a French expeditionary force defeated the volunteers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a>, who were trying to seize Rome. The victory, aided by the new French Chassepot rifle, kept Rome under the pope until 1870.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mentana">Battle of Mentana</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Laika becomes the first animal to orbit the Earth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> launched the dog Laika aboard Sputnik 2. She died within hours from overheating, but the flight showed a living creature could survive launch and weightlessness.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 3 November <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stephen-f-austin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stephen-f-austin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stephen F. Austin</span><span class="tp">1793–1836</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/carlos-ibanez-del-campo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carlos-ibanez-del-campo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Carlos Ibáñez del Campo</span><span class="tp">1877–1960</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfredo-stroessner"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfredo-stroessner.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfredo Stroessner</span><span class="tp">1912–2006</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/valdas-adamkus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/valdas-adamkus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Valdas Adamkus</span><span class="tp">b. 1926</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 3 November <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pirmin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pirmin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Saint Pirmin</span><span class="tp">c. 670–753</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-iii-doukas-vatatzes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-iii-doukas-vatatzes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John III Doukas Vatatzes</span><span class="tp">c. 1192–1254</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-borromeo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-borromeo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles Borromeo</span><span class="tp">1538–1584</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-de-porres"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-de-porres.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martin de Porres</span><span class="tp">1579–1639</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
